coolify:index/apiSettings:ApiSettings.description:
Manages Coolify instance-level settings: the REST API and the MCP server. Requires a root team (team 0) API token. On destroy, the API is re-enabled (to prevent lockout) and the MCP server is disabled.

## Example Usage

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as coolify from "@pulumi/coolify";

// Enable the Coolify REST API and MCP server.
const main = new coolify.ApiSettings("main", {
    enabled: true,
    mcpEnabled: true,
});
```
```python
import pulumi
import pulumi_coolify as coolify

# Enable the Coolify REST API and MCP server.
main = coolify.ApiSettings("main",
    enabled=True,
    mcp_enabled=True)
```
```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using Pulumi;
using Coolify = Pulumi.Coolify;

return await Deployment.RunAsync(() => 
{
    // Enable the Coolify REST API and MCP server.
    var main = new Coolify.ApiSettings("main", new()
    {
        Enabled = true,
        McpEnabled = true,
    });

});
```
```go
package main

import (
	"github.com/mheers/pulumi-provider-coolify/sdk/go/coolify"
	"github.com/pulumi/pulumi/sdk/v3/go/pulumi"
)

func main() {
	pulumi.Run(func(ctx *pulumi.Context) error {
		// Enable the Coolify REST API and MCP server.
		_, err := coolify.NewApiSettings(ctx, "main", &coolify.ApiSettingsArgs{
			Enabled:    pulumi.Bool(true),
			McpEnabled: pulumi.Bool(true),
		})
		if err != nil {
			return err
		}
		return nil
	})
}
```
```hcl
pulumi {
  required_providers {
    coolify = {
      source = "pulumi/coolify"
    }
  }
}

# Enable the Coolify REST API and MCP server.
resource "coolify_apisettings" "main" {
  enabled     = true
  mcp_enabled = true
}
```
```java
