coolify:index/application:Application.description:
Manages a Coolify application deployed from a **public** Git repository.

This resource is for public HTTPS Git URLs only. A private repository will fail to clone (for example `fatal: could not read Username for 'https://github.com'`).

For private sources, use:
- <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`coolify.ApplicationPrivateGit`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`coolify.ApplicationPrivateGit`" pulumi-lang-go="`ApplicationPrivateGit`" pulumi-lang-python="`ApplicationPrivateGit`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`coolify.ApplicationPrivateGit`" pulumi-lang-java="`coolify.ApplicationPrivateGit`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`coolify_application_private_git`">`coolify.ApplicationPrivateGit`</span> with an SSH deploy key
- <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`coolify.ApplicationGithubApp`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`coolify.ApplicationGithubApp`" pulumi-lang-go="`ApplicationGithubApp`" pulumi-lang-python="`ApplicationGithubApp`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`coolify.ApplicationGithubApp`" pulumi-lang-java="`coolify.ApplicationGithubApp`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`coolify_application_github_app`">`coolify.ApplicationGithubApp`</span> with a GitHub App

See the Which application resource do I use? guide.

## Example Usage

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as coolify from "@pulumi/coolify";

const example = new coolify.Application("example", {
    name: "my-web-app",
    projectUuid: exampleCoolifyProject.uuid,
    serverUuid: exampleCoolifyServer.uuid,
    gitRepository: "https://github.com/example/app",
    gitBranch: "main",
    buildPack: "nixpacks",
    portsExposes: "3000",
    domains: "https://app.example.com",
});
